INT. PLANETARIUM DOME, CITY MUSEUM - NIGHT

A hush of velvet seats under a black ceiling stippled with fake stars. A projector as big as a refrigerator squats in the centre like a sleeping insect.

LUCIEN DAGGETT, fifties, tuxedoed, courteous, once a stage magician, kneels at the projector with a screwdriver. MAEVE OSHIRO, thirties, in a night-guard uniform two sizes too large, holds a flashlight and a walkie-talkie. FELIX BRANDT, twenty, wiry, in black, dangles from a rope through a hatch in the dome.

LUCIEN
Is the corridor clear?

MAEVE
Clear for four minutes.

LUCIEN
Felix. Descend.

FELIX
I'm descending!

The rope pays out. Felix swings across the dome, sneakers squeaking, and plants one foot on a seat back and the other on the projector, and the whole machine tilts. Lucien and Maeve both lunge to steady it. The three of them end up in a knot, Felix's rope wrapped round Maeve's arm, Lucien's screwdriver pinned under Felix's chin. A hidden lens flares, and a thousand stars wheel across the ceiling.

MAEVE
Get off me.

FELIX
I can't, you're on the rope.

LUCIEN
Both of you, be still.

They hold still. A tiny brass drawer slides out of the projector's base. Inside lies a velvet pouch.

LUCIEN (CONT'D)
There you are.

MAEVE
That's it? That's the Orion Diamond?

LUCIEN
That's it.

A door slams somewhere in the museum. Footsteps. All three freeze. The stars keep turning overhead. Then Lucien smiles, and tucks the pouch into his cummerbund.
